$ apprafter top
[exit 0]
[stdout]

Node solo-1 — Ready · schedulable
 RESOURCE   CAPACITY   ALLOCATABLE   REQUESTED   SCHEDULABLE   IN-USE   FREE 
 CPU        2          1.9           400m        1.5           —        —    
 Memory     3.7Gi      3.2Gi         704Mi       2.5Gi         —        —    
 Disk       39Gi       37Gi          0           37Gi          11Gi     26Gi 

Workload breakdown — 3 pods, cluster-wide
 BUCKET                PODS   CPU REQ   CPU USE   MEM REQ   MEM USE   DISK REQ   DISK USE 
 platform              1      100m      —         128Mi     —         0          512Ki    
 integrated services   1      250m      —         512Mi     —         0          512Ki    
 applications          1      50m       —         64Mi      —         0          512Ki    
 other                 0      0m        —         0         —         0          0        
 TOTAL                 3      400m      —         704Mi     —         0          1.5Mi    

SCHEDULABLE is allocatable − requested: what a new pod could still ask for.
FREE is allocatable − in-use: what is unused right now. A node can be fully requested
and barely used, or barely requested and full; these two columns are what tells them apart.

CPU and memory IN-USE / FREE read `—` because nothing was measured. `metrics.k8s.io`
answered:
  Error from server (NotFound): the server could not find the requested resource
Install or repair metrics-server (`kubectl top` reads the same API). CAPACITY, ALLOCATABLE,
REQUESTED and SCHEDULABLE come from the node and pod specs and are unaffected.

Disk is `ephemeral-storage` — the node's root filesystem. The node's IN-USE is the whole
filesystem (OS, container images, logs and volume data included), so it is larger than the
DISK USE column, which counts only each pod's writable layer, logs and emptyDir volumes.
